      "description": "Mediaeval garden outline Those who had houses along Linlithgow High Street in mediaeval times had a narrow strip of land the width of their property leading down to the Loch. This let them grow crops for their own use. Most of these characteristic properties have been altered or destroyed in the centuries since but several gardens to the west of Linlithgow Palace retain their mediaeval form. The garden stretches almost 100 metres from the lochside path to the High Street but is only some 5 metres wide.",
